+# Strict PHYLIP input decoder handoff
+
+This records a narrow implementation for the parent's frozen decoder ports.
+The original user attachment remains authoritative. This is not a goal, scope
+amendment, native conformance receipt, completed integration, or live-resource
+claim. No fixed inventory/status row is changed.
+
+Owned production file: `gene_annotation_episode/hmmer_alignment_input_phylip.py`.
+Owned test file: `tests/test_hmmer_alignment_input_phylip.py`.
+Public API: `decode_native_phylip_alignment(content: bytes, *,
+declared_format: str, alphabet: str) -> dict`, restricted to `phylip`/`phylips`
+and `amino`/`DNA`/`RNA`. The result is the frozen DecoderBatch, using the existing
+shared byte iterator and seven-field diagnostic constructor. No schema change,
+alphabet inference, numerical sheet, weights, checksum, MAP, driver, views,
+prompt, library, literature or credit implementation is included.
+
+## Source inspection
+
+Complete relevant functions were read from the retained Infernal 1.1.5 source.
+Hashes and explicit function anchors are in `EVIDENCE.json`.
+
+- `esl_msafile_phylip.c`: SetInmap, GuessAlphabet, Read,
+  phylip_interleaved_Read, phylip_sequential_Read,
+  phylip_rectify_input_name. Declared input uses exactly ten name bytes; relaxed
+  format autodetection and output writer behavior do not define this decoder.
+- `esl_mem.c`: esl_mem_strtoi32, esl_memtok, esl_memspn, esl_memnewline.
+- `esl_alphabet.c`: Create/CreateCustom, create_rna/create_dna/create_amino,
+  SetEquiv/SetCaseInsensitive, esl_abc_dsqcat and esl_abc_dsqcat_noalloc.
+- `esl_msa.c`: esl_msa_SetSeqName. `esl_msafile.c`: GetLine/PutLine.
+  `esl_buffer.c`: GetLine and buffer_countline.
+
+The source rules distinguish 0–8 from forbidden 9, `? -> ~`, nucleic uppercase
+`O -> -` from illegal lowercase `o`, and amino O/o residues. Sequence NUL is a
+defined alias to X (amino) or N (DNA/RNA); space/tab/NUL-only lines are blank
+where the native memspn scanner is applied. Names trim literal spaces and replace
+internal spaces with underscores; duplicate or empty transformed names retain
+separate positional rows. Source names that reach non-ASCII C ctype remain
+unavailable. Sequence high bytes reach the defined digital isascii rejection.
+
+The base-0 integer implementation accepts native numeric prefixes, octal and
+lowercase 0x, and preserves the signed int32 range and overflow rejection. It
+never substitutes Python decimal/full-token parsing. Nonpositive dimensions
+remain explicit source-semantics unavailable, before unsafe allocation/reading.
+Only high bytes actually examined by the source converter invoke the ctype
+limitation; suffix bytes after an earlier ASCII terminator remain ignored.
+
+## Data and failure meanings
+
+Events retain every consumed physical line, including its original LF/CRLF
+terminator. Segments retain valid consumed symbols and ignored payload spans,
+with zero-based half-open byte/physical-column/aligned coordinates. On an invalid
+sequence byte, validated prefix segments remain; the complete rejected line,
+including its remaining bytes, remains in its Event. No invalid byte is replaced
+by a manufactured successful residue. No failed alignment is padded.
+
+`column_count` is the completed interleaved-block width, or the final PHYLIPS
+row width when the native reader reaches its successful return. A failed
+PHYLIPS read has no assigned final native alignment width, so that field stays
+null; exact attempted row widths remain in strings and segments. An unfinished
+interleaved block does not increment block_count. PHYLIPS block_count is null.
+Rows may retain locally valid partial spans, but a partial/invalid record is not
+a successful scientific alignment.
+
+A PHYLIP overwidth record followed by nonblank lookahead retains native status
+0, both widths, and invalid geometry; the same overwidth at EOF retains native
+status 7. PHYLIPS final-row EOF skips the source width check, so unequal or
+short/long/zero-width final rows retain status 0 and invalid geometry. These
+statuses are source equivalents, not observed returncodes. Known unsafe native
+array/MAP paths have not been executed.
+
+Successful final nonblank lookahead is put back and belongs to the next record;
+trailing blanks belong to the current record. A PHYLIPS overwidth error with a
+nonblank following line has already consumed that lookahead and does not put it
+back: its raw invalid Event and cursor preserve that fact. Later malformed
+records never erase an earlier complete record. Empty/initial-blank-only input
+has no alignment occurrence. Complete population is decoded without a fixed
+record or line sampling limit.
